refs reports every corpus member whose body or registered frontmatter properties reference the given slug. Qualified by an anchor, written <slug>#<anchor>, it reports only the references whose anchor resolves to that heading — the blast radius of renaming it — and a reference whose anchor matches more than one heading is reported for each, marked as matching more than one. A heading is matched on its identifier, so letter case and punctuation do not decide a match. Given --outbound, it reports the documents that slug references instead; --outbound takes no anchor. A slug no corpus member declares is reported distinctly from one that is declared but unreferenced; both exit zero, as does an anchor nothing references. The answer is compact by default — one entry per referring document, each reference reduced to its line and text — and --full returns every field of every reference, its span included.

Usage:
  specs refs <slug>[#<anchor>] [flags]

Flags:
      --full       report every field of every reference, its span included, instead of the compact view
  -h, --help       help for refs
      --json       write the references as JSON instead of YAML
      --outbound   report the documents the slug references, instead of the documents referencing it

Global Flags:
      --config string   path to the repository's specs.toml (default "specs.toml")
